WEBVTT

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.200
<i>To save the Food Research Club,</i>

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.500
<i>the invaluable place where he could spend time with his closest, long-time female friend,</i>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>Oojima Yuuki decided to take part in the election.</i>

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:25.180
<i>In response to his feelings, his friend agreed to help him with his campaign to the best of her ability,</i>

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.170
<i>together with her best friends.</i>

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.980
Okay! That's all 3,600 Yaoi Stick-pamphlets!

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.940
Yuuki, make sure you get those Oojima Rolls baked by the end of the day.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.140
Got it.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.970
I'll do my best on writing the speech.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.970
Can you handle it, Mifuyu?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.580
Let us know if it's too much.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.980
Yuuki will pull an all-nighter to work on it.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>I</i> will?

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.650
It's all right. I can manage on my own.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.820
Thank you, Mifuyu!

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.700
I'm so glad that you're on our side.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:57.820
I'm in love with you.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.650
Will you go out with me?

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.800
I'm flattered, Yuu-kun,

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.000
but I'm in love with someone else.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.830
Impossible!

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.220
Too bad!

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.420
There's no place in her heart for you!

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.710
Oh, no!

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.220
You're at it <i>again</i>?

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.480
You all get along so well.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.970
One thing led to another and...

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.660
Really?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.220
You looked rather excited to me.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.220
Chisato does love Yuu-kun, after all.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.160
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.650
There's no way I'd fall in love with this idiot!

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.150
No kidding. You can tell that much
from how she works me like a slave.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:37.000
Ouch!

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.560
What's wrong with you?!

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.260
You're so hopeless, Yuu-kun.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.020
What? Me?

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.240
Why me?

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.900
You're just so hopleless.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.440
What exactly makes me hopeless?

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.080
I wonder.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.970
<i>Yuuki's insecure nature may have caused him to show indifference toward her when in public,</i>

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.470
<i>but deep down inside, just like in the earlier skit...</i>

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.440
Wh-Why are you strangling me?!

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.800
President, please tell me!
he was... in love with Mifuyu.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.640
Tell me!
he was... in love with Mifuyu.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.520
he was... in love with Mifuyu.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.350
Yuuki-senpai?

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.980
Yuuki-senpai!

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.860
All right, time to get baking!

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.540
Do your best, Yuu-kun.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.620
This isn't a problem for you, is it?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.710
What do you mean?

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.800
I can afford to skip a few classes,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.470
but isn't your attendance at risk of being too low?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.860
It's all right.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.220
I've been in good health lately, so I haven't been absent all that much.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.860
I see. That's a relief.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:13.020
This is also my chance to repay Chisato for the favor she did for me.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.230
A favor?

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.980
It's thanks to Chisato that I can be here today, having fun.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.490
Mii-chan...

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:26.860
When I transferred to this school after being held back for a year due to surgery,

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.750
everyone was so careful around me
because I was a year older than them.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.180
They used respectful language and treated me like I was special.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:37.320
I felt out of place in my own class.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.880
It was both stressful and painful.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.040
Then Chisato came along and saved me.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:43.930
Need a hand?

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.480
Oh, thanks.
She doesn't even think about stuff like that,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.540
She doesn't even think about stuff like that,

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.760
so she's able to talk casually with anyone.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:53.520
Still, it was thanks to her that I started to fit in.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.920
I'm really grateful.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.600
That's why I want to help her out however I can.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.440
I'll do my best to save the
Food Club she holds so dearly.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.500
Yeah. We'll do our best together.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.840
Okay, that's two down.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.400
That's awe-Samantha, Tabitha!

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.940
Um... What?

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:45.490
Those were the names of a witch and her daughter on an old TV show. You've never heard of them?

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:48.420
Why do you know something that old?

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.440
I'm a year older than you, remember?

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.620
I don't think a year would make a difference there...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.130
And that makes six done.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.520
Mii-chan, what time is it?

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.460
Just beef-ore the hour!

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.390
Another old joke?

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.510
From the ramen ad with dancing cows.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.480
I don't get it.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.300
Excuse me.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.280
I am Shiohama Hidaka, a reporter with the ASP.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.940
I'm currently compiling a directory of presidential candidates,

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.400
and if you don't mind, I would like to interview you.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:29.940
S-Sure.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:30.980
Go on.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:32.660
To begin...

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.160
Your name is Ooshima Yuuki, correct?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.910
No. My family name is Oojima.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.860
Excuse the mistake.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.500
So it's Ooshima...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.980
No, I told you that it's Oojima!

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.670
No need to repeat yourself.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.680
But you just pronounced it as "Ooshima"!

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.440
I'm short on time, so let's move on.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.680
What is the key policy of your campaign, Mr. Ooshima?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.740
You're still calling me Ooshima!

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.100
Please answer the question.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.680
Correct my name first.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.570
That's the most important thing for the election!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.880
So that's the most important.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.070
His key policy is the correction of his name.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.560
That's not what I meant!

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.080
Lastly, do you have a message for the voters?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.450
Don't just skip the rest!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.940
"Don't just skip the rest!"

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.140
That wasn't the message!

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.420
That's all for the interview.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.620
Thank you very much for your time.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:25.710
Hey, wait!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.120
You misunderstood me!

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:36.900
"Please support my campaign."

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:40.780
"Thank you very much for listening."

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.880
That makes eight.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.230
How are you holding up, Mii-chan?

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:48.380
Yeah, I just finished...

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.490
Actually, I think it'll take a while longer.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:53.490
Okay. Hang in there.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:54.990
Yeah!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.180
How are things coming along, Yuuki-senpai?

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.870
Well, we should be able to make it.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.680
What about you?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:09.220
Well, I swung by to see you
produce some sticky, white stuff.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.420
What the hell?

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.800
Oh, Yuuki-senpai...

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.280
Your sweet, white cream.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.600
Hey!

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.020
Delicious!

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:38.800
<i>Yuuki worked on the cakes slowly so that he could spend more time with Mifuyu.</i>

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:44.060
<i>The two were there, together in peace.</i>

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.420
Good morning, everybody!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.100
What's up, Non-chan-senpai?

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.800
Yuu-chan, my junior, do you know what an "angel's share" is?

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:59.800
It's the portion of alcohol that naturally evaporates in the aging barrel, isn't it?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.440
That's exactly right!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:08.310
So you're aware that one Oojima Roll
out of every ten is an angels' share, right?

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.280
Who's the angel in this case?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.540
That'd be the one loved by everyone, Non-chan!

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.700
The angel here for her share!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.700
There aren't any here for you today, Non-chan.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.180
I'll bake one for you next time, so forget about it for—

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:34.120
O-Okay! I'll give you the ends, so please don't!

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:37.840
You're giving Non-chan the ends from all 20 rolls?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.240
Yes, I am.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.220
I'm busy right now, so please come back when I'm done.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.560
You really are a true-blue friend!

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.600
A blue bosom buddy!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.840
<i>Yuuki and Mifuyu shared a slice from one end.</i>

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:02.840
<i>It was sweet and warm, just like
the time they had spent together.</i>

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.870
Just a few more!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.000
Should I make some tea, Yuu-kun?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.280
Oh, could you? That'd be great.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.000
You got it!

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.430
Hi!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:21.430
Yuu-kun, how are things going?

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.580
Sensei, you're a little too close.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.380
What did you come here for?

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.300
Could you be any meaner?

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.690
I'm here because I care about you.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.900
You haven't come over to cook for me since you launched your campaign.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.660
I'm lonely!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.340
I can't help it! I'm busy!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.920
Oh, I almost forgot!

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.920
I have some business to take care of.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.880
What's up with that clichéd excuse?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.130
Later. Good luck, Yuu-kun.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:02.430
Yuu-kun, could you do me a favor?

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.390
I don't want you to get distracted.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.770
Pay more attention to Chisato.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.700
That again?

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.360
I want both of you to be happy.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.440
You mean you want Chisato to be happy, right?

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:24.120
Don't worry. I'm looking right at her in my own way.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:25.620
Yuu-kun...

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:29.960
Excuse me!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.560
I was dispatched from the Election Administration Committee!

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:34.040
My name is Aomi Isara!

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:35.560
You're...

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.820
Aomi-san!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.550
Dispatched?

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:44.550
A financial aid student is assigned to
each candidate for errands and the like.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.920
Then you're my...

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:52.160
Yes! I'll be helping you from now until the end of your campaign!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:54.060
I'm glad to be able to work with you!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:12:01.200
It's an amazing coincidence that I was matched up with you when there are over a hundred candidates.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.060
Yeah, really.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:05.760
This could be fate.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.700
Just kidding!

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.280
That's...

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.250
<i>Oops.</i>

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.860
A-Anyway, let's do our best!

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:17.860
Right! I'll be giving it my all!

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.930
<b>Takafuji High School
Primary Election</b>

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.310
Everyone, it's a pleasure to be working with you!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.940
Likewise. Help make Yuuki win!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.690
Of course! I'll give it my best!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.780
But man, we're lucky to have landed a spot right next to the event stage.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.540
The president arranged it for us.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:49.480
Oh, that's our president for you!

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.450
Guys!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.040
It's starting soon!

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:03.050
Takafuji Private Academy's
primary election begins now!

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.300
No running!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.930
Please keep things moving!

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:10.020
Stay in an orderly line, please!

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.180
Don't push!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.060
It's so lively.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.820
Is it like this every year?

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:17.440
Look.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.840
I'll take one of each poster!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.960
Shinonome-san's manifesto audio CD, please!

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.300
Give me ten of them!

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.940
She's so popular.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.820
Just what you'd expect from the Finance Commission.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.330
We're back!

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.160
Where have you guys been?

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.910
We got some campaign goods!

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.640
Aren't they goods from other candidates?

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.260
Why are you helping the enemy?

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.840
It's fine. Just think of it as a little reconnaissance.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.380
So whose goods did you get?

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.900
So obvious...

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:50.980
This looks ridiculous!

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:52.620
No less from the General Affairs Commission.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:53.220
Huh?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.100
They're pretty good.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.520
They'll be tough to beat.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.520
Tough to beat? This guy?

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.980
You're selling goods here, Ariake, Garage?

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:10.700
It's in return for them being the
President and VP of your support group!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.860
Wait. You didn't know?

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.950
You're the one who made that backroom deal!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.540
I'll be selling figures and garage kits,

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:21.160
and Ariake-shi will be selling doujinshi.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.100
We don't have enough space in our club stall!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.390
Oojima Yuuki<b>
</b>Food Research Club

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:27.560
All right, guys! Are you ready?

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.440
People will be pouring in soon!

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.280
Yuuki, you go get ready for the speech!

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.800
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:36.200
Crap, I left the script at home!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.100
What? You haven't memorized it?

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:42.120
There's no way I could memorize a script that long!

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.020
I need to go over it at least one more time before the speech!

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:47.820
I have the file, so I'll go print another copy.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.280
Sorry about this. You're a lifesaver, Mii-chan.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:50.880
You can count on me.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.200
All right, guys. Let's do this!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.330
Please support Oojima Yuuki!

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.520
Please support Oojima Yuuki!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.210
Please vote for Yuu-chan, or Oojima Yuuki!

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:07.340
O...

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.100
Oojima...

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.960
Vote for Oojima.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.390
Keep at it, Morishita-san!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.020
Please line up here!

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:25.040
The newest one and England x America!

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.610
Okay, the newest one and England x America!

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:29.040
That'll be 2,000 yen!

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.910
Don't forget to vote for Oojima Yuuki!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.020
Snakes and crabs, two each.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.900
Two sets of snakes and crabs!

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:38.330
That will be 13,000 yen!

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.700
Make sure to vote for Oojima Yuuki!

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.590
O-Okay! I will.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.860
It was the right choice to have those two sell goods.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:48.740
Wasn't it?

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.090
Oojima...

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.220
Oojima... Pamphlet.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.720
Vote... Please.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.700
She's improved!

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:01.350
The real deal begins when
we start selling Oojima Rolls!

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:03.850
Done!

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.660
"Yuuki gently embraced Mifuyu,

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.150
and their lips..."

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:12.030
Wait. Why did I print this one?

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:16.100
What am I so flustered about?

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:21.210
Oh, no! I need to hurry and print the script for the speech!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:25.640
The super popular Oojima Roll is now on sale!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:27.340
It's 300 yen per slice!

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:28.900
300 yen?!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.900
We said that even 190 was pushing it, so why?

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:38.020
It was Chii-chan's idea. A cosplayer of the buyer's choice will feed it to them!

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:39.720
That makes it worth 300 yen?

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.480
Can you two link arms?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.270
Wait a second!

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.520
If you want to take photos of us...

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:56.060
...buy an Oojima Roll bundled with the photo ticket!

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:57.940
Then we'll take...

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.410
...any pose you want!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.240
Starting at 500 yen each!

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.250
Oojima Roll!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.920
It's 500 yen with the photo ticket?

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:08.880
What do you think?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:09.480
Huh?

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.400
I came up with the cosplay idea!

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:13.670
Isn't it working pretty well?

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:15.940
Wh-What's with the getup?!

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:17.680
Don't I look adorable?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.460
Hey, I could see your underwear!

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.460
It's okay! It's just my swimsuit!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.060
Does that really make a difference?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.540
Chisato, you're up!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:28.440
Coming!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:31.220
Yuuki-senpai!

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:31.730
Hm?

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.990
What do you think about my dress?

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.700
N-Not you, too!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.320
He's kind of cute!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.200
He looks like a girl!

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.760
That's the guy, right?

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:43.700
And <i>that</i> one is the...

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:45.120
What's with them?

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.080
Yumeshima-kun, Ooshima-kun,

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.620
you're up next!

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:49.580
For what?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.380
What <i>is</i> this?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.630
Just stand there and feed each other.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.220
Say, "Open up!"

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.760
Like this, please!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.000
What the hell is this?

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.020
That looks like you and me.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:07.920
We sold them for 1,000 yen each, special requests included.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.400
I'm counting on you guys!

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.320
Guess we have no choice.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.940
You look way too happy about this!

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.190
This is all to collect campaign funds!

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.450
Anyway, open up!

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.040
This is so hot!

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.620
He's a tsundere!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.620
W-Was that good enough?

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:33.210
I'm prepared to take requests for this page if it's for the campaign.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.660
What do you think, everyone?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:36.090
Do it!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.880
Hell no!

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.800
We're now checking in candidates who wish to give a speech.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.480
Those interested should come to the EAC office located below the stage.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:49.920
So it's time.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:52.160
Yuuki, you're up.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.080
But I don't have the script yet.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.230
Yuu-kun!

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:00.320
Sorry I took so long.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:04.120
It's fine. It's Yuuki's fault for forgetting.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:06.080
Here you go.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.800
Thank you, Mii-chan!

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:10.830
I really do love you!

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.770
Um...

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:14.040
I...

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:19.060
Oh, I mean, I'm in love with someone else.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:21.620
Too bad! There's no place in her—

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:24.060
Wait! We don't have time to fool around!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.300
There's a place for you over there!

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:27.720
Right!

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:29.600
Hold on!

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:33.680
All right!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:37.700
Kiss!

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.560
Get going!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.400
All done, Mr. Ooshima. That way, please.

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:55.540
It's Oojima.

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:03.520
So you're Mr. Oojima?

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.050
Huh?

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:10.520
I'm Tatsumi Moheiji, the candidate endorsed by the General Affairs Commission.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.310
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.060
O-Okay.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.680
If I'm not mistaken, your Food Club manifesto

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:20.570
aims to preserve the freedom that club activities currently have.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:24.820
I take it that it's in opposition to the Finance Commission manifesto?

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:26.340
Yes.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:31.960
I see! My policies and your platform are in perfect alignment.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.760
I'd appreciate your support after the primaries.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:36.660
Huh?

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:40.670
We share an anti-Shinonome stance.

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.960
We're thinking along the same lines.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:46.090
No, I don't intend to end my campaign at the primaries.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:50.540
I entered this race to win.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.940
I intend to make it through the primaries,

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:54.350
so I won't be able to support you afterward.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:01.360
Far be it from me to stop you.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:05.400
You should follow the path that you believe in.

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:06.500
However...

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.370
"However"?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:12.140
However, you might find yourself at a dead end.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:16.370
Should that happen, I'll be there to guide you.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:20.130
Please support me when that time comes.

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:24.130
Mr. Tatsumi, you're up next.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.620
I wish you the best of luck. Until next time.

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:31.390
That bastard...

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:35.410
Good work!

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:36.280
Please support Oojima Yuuki!
Good work!

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.360
Are you feeling all right?
Please support Oojima Yuuki!

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:38.080
Yeah, I'm fine. Thanks.
Please support Oojima Yuuki!

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.720
Yeah, I'm fine. Thanks.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:41.270
Relax for the time being!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.960
I guess I'll have to throw this away at home.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:59.420
Th-This is the script for the speech!

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:02.090
That means I gave Yuu-kun the...

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:23.540
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:27.490
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:31.590
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:35.670
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:40.010
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:44.180
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:48.100
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:54.690
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:56.350 --> 00:23:01.330
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:05.500
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:07.730
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:11.380
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.910
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:18.180
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:22.050
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:27.810
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:35.690
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:45.570
Snacks are delicious, but they can be scary when you have to watch your weight!

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:48.720
It's surprising how some snacks are really high in calories.

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:51.860
A bag of potato chips has as many calories as a bowl of soba noodles, for instance!

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:54.660
It's easy to go way over a standard meal if you snack without thinking!

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.510
There are low-calorie snacks that can help!

00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:58.300
Like what?

00:23:58.300 --> 00:23:59.080
Tell us!

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:01.760
Agar jelly, konjac jelly, and <i>tokoroten</i>!

00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:03.960
They're all wobbly!

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:06.200
Next time, Episode 6: Results.

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:09.280
Whoa! My belly fat started going all jiggly!
